 "text": "Property Tax Payments\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nHistory\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's\nOffice\nHomestead Exemptions\nPersonal Property Info\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary\nDischarge\nProperty Valuation\nProtests\nSpecial\nLicenses\nCounty Court\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict\nCourt Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's\nOffice\nElection Information\nSecretary of State\nLocal\nElection Results\nEmergency Manager\nExtension Office\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of\nDeeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's\nOffice\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's\nExam\nDrivers Licenses\nFAQ's\nProperty Tax Payments\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nCommunity\nLinks\nServices Offered\nFeedback\n-->\nTax Payments\nWhen are real property taxes due?\nReal property taxes are due December 31. The first half\nof the tax becomes delinquent on the following May 1 and the\nsecond half becomes delinquent on September 1.\nWhen are personal property taxes due?\nPersonal property taxes are due December 31. The first\nhalf of the tax becomes delinquent on the following May 1\nand the second half becomes delinquent on September 1.\nOn the due date, the taxes become a first lien on all\npersonal property you own. If the taxes are not paid, any\npersonal property you own, whether taxable or not, is\nsubject to seizure in order to satisfy the lien.\nCopyright © 2010 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
